# GitHub builds its "Download ZIP" and release source archives with
# `git archive`, which honours these. Anything marked here is kept out of
# that download, so what lands in the browser profile is the extension and
# nothing else — no README sitting in the extension folder, no build script,
# no icon generator.
#
# `git clone` ignores export-ignore entirely, so contributors still get
# everything. LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md are deliberately absent
# from this list: MIT requires them to travel with the code.

README.md         export-ignore
.gitattributes    export-ignore
.gitignore        export-ignore
.claude/          export-ignore
tools/            export-ignore
icons/generate.py export-ignore
icons/logo512.png export-ignore
